index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..647fee825a779467ce68dbed9b82072bb6273e2d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@
+# Generalized MinRank points from arXiv:1112.4411
+
+Status: the generator passes local gates G1--G8, but it is **not shippable yet**.
+The required four-vendor hardening run reached OpenRouter and received `403 Key
+limit exceeded` on every retry. Those calls remain in the script-owned
+`llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`; they are errors, not model failures. G9 and the
+shipping rung therefore remain unmeasured, and `selftest_report.json` correctly
+records `all_passed=false`.
+
+| Profile field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | B -- no-tool compression |
+| Native domain | algebra |
+| Object regime | finite field |
+| Computational core | linear algebra |
+| Certificate form | integer tuple (a native finite-field point) |
+| Intended intuition | change of variables |
+| Domain essentiality | native |
+| Reduction | none |
+
+## The problem
+
+The source is Faugère, Safey El Din, and Spaenlehauer, [*On the
+Complexity of the Generalized MinRank Problem*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.4411).
+Section 1 defines generalized MinRank: given a polynomial matrix over a field,
+find points where its evaluation has rank at most a stated bound. This family
+hands the solver exactly such an affine matrix over a prime field. It uses
+square size `d+1`, rank bound 1, degree 1, and `k=d^2`, so
+`k=(n-r)(m-r)`, the paper's zero-dimensional regime.
+
+Generation first draws a pairwise-distinct finite-field point `S`. It chooses a
+random assignment of variable names and random signs on Walsh characters, then
+constructs the constant block so that the active block is `H D (X-S)`. A final
+isolated entry equal to 1 makes the full evaluated matrix have rank at most 1
+exactly when the active block is zero. This is inverse generation: no solver is
+run to obtain the planted point. Checking a candidate substitutes its residues
+and tests exact finite-field rank; `verify` never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+This is not a Track A claim. Section 6 explicitly solves zero-dimensional
+MinRank loci by forming `(r+1)`-minors, computing a grevlex Gröbner basis with
+F5, and converting it with FGLM. Theorem 5 bounds that method for generic affine
+matrices. Section 7 identifies parameter families where its arithmetic cost is
+polynomial in the degree, and Table 1 reports FGb and Magma timings. The paper's
+finite-field NP-completeness statement is worst-case and says nothing about this
+planted distribution.
+
+For this structured specialization, the anchor minors are 64 linear equations.
+The executable reference algorithm performs ordinary modular Gaussian
+elimination in `O(k^3)` field operations and solves 8/8 shipping instances. The
+measured seed uses 23,976 field operations and about 0.0021 s (maximum 24,648
+operations in the eight-run panel). That is easy for a tool and unrealistic by
+hand. The compact route recognizes signed columns of the Walsh basis, shares
+butterfly sums across all coordinates, and uses exactly 256 additions or
+scalings. Its arithmetic fits the no-tool cap; recognizing the common basis in
+the expanded matrix is the intended challenge.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+For `make_instance(n=11, dimension=2, seed=11)`, the full matrix is
+
+```text
+M(x) = [ 8-x2-x3    4-x0-x1   0 ]
+       [ 1-x2+x3   10-x0+x1   0 ]   over F_11.
+       [    0          0       1 ]
+```
+
+The required bound is 1, variables and coordinates are 0-indexed, and the four
+coordinates must be distinct canonical residues. The answer is
+
+```text
+<answer>[7, 8, 10, 9]</answer>
+```
+
+`verify(inst, [7, 8, 10, 9])` returns `(True, "ok")`. Dropping the last
+coordinate returns `(False, "point must contain exactly 4 coordinates")`.
+A person can solve this demo by setting the four active affine entries to zero;
+the higher presets expand the same idea enough that elimination is no longer a
+reasonable by-hand route.
+
+## Difficulty presets
+
+| Preset | Field lower bound `n` | `d` | Variables | Status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 11 | 2 | 4 | hand-solvable illustration |
+| easy | 1009 | 4 | 16 | oracle run blocked before a verdict |
+| medium | 1009 | 8 | 64 | provisional shipping preset |
+| hard | 65521 | 8 | 64 | fixed answer length, wider arithmetic |
+
+Increasing `d` grows the equation system; increasing `n` grows the field and
+answer entropy without adding coordinates. `escalate()` continues along the
+fixed-length field-size axis and reports `cap_bound` before serialized residues
+can exceed the output contract.
+
+## Local gates
+
+| Gate | Result | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses verify across all presets |
+| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged JSON recovered from prose and a markdown fence |
+| G4 | pass | 0 hits / 200,000 structure-aware injective points |
+| G5 | pass | demo: exactly 1/7,920; shipping density 0/200,000; reference 23,976 operations |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks at 0/8 each; reference elimination solves 8/8 |
+| G7 | pass | field 1009 to 2027 adds 66 search-space bits with 64 coordinates |
+| G8 | pass | 60 invariance and 60 carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9 | **not run** | 320 chars, 64 atoms, about 80 tokens; verified compact route 256 operations |
+
+The four failing G6 probes are a per-variable coefficient-support outlier,
+single-equation greedy assignment, 256 uniform injective restarts, and an
+in-context Walsh ansatz that ignores the randomized variable/sign alignment.
+The successful Gaussian reference is separate, as Track B requires.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+The bare loop wrote four error rows at the first easy rung and then stopped as
+required; no call is counted as an attempt or failure.
+
+| Preset | Vendors reached | Valid attempts | Result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| easy | Claude Sonnet 5, Grok 4.6 | 0 | repeated HTTP 403 key-limit errors |
+
+| G9 arm | Solved / attempts | Conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0 / 0 | not measured |
+| hinted | 0 / 0 | not measured; G9(b) does not pass |
+| placebo | 0 / 0 | not measured |
+
+The hinted-minus-placebo value is recorded as 0 only because both denominators
+are zero; it supports no inference. Once quota is restored, rerun the bare
+ladder, set `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` to the held rung, rerun the local gates, and
+run the hinted and placebo copies in separate scratch directories.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import gen_1112_4411 as g
+
+params = g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=123, **params)
+statement = g.render(inst)
+answer = g.parse_answer("<answer>" + __import__("json").dumps(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>")
+assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After all oracle gates pass, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1112.4411
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- This result is blocked on external oracle quota. It must not be submitted or
+  counted as hardened from the current transcript.
+- The generated matrices are deliberately nongeneric. Theorem 5 describes the
+  paper's generic mechanical route, not a hardness theorem for this distribution.
+  The family-specific linear reference is therefore the honest Track B baseline.
+- G4 samples uniformly from the stated pairwise-distinct point language. Zero
+  hits bounds that prior; it is not, by itself, evidence of computational
+  hardness. Construction proves uniqueness, and exact enumeration confirms it
+  only at the demo size.
+- The full F5/FGLM implementation and production Gröbner-basis packages were not
+  available or needed: anchor-minor extraction collapses this specialization to
+  exact linear elimination. Such tools are expected to solve it.
+- The adversary panel does not try every basis-learning or tensor-decomposition
+  attack. A solver that detects the signed Walsh factors can solve the family;
+  that is the intended insight.
+- `canonical_key` is exact for variable renaming and arbitrary row/column
+  permutations, which G8 tests compositionally. It uses a strong cheap invariant,
+  not a complete canonical form for all left/right `GL` equivalences, so it may
+  miss more general rank-preserving isomorphisms or theoretically collide.
